fact WorkItem(id: "WI-213", description: some(value: "scaland mirror of `anthill-smt-gen` emitter — emit SMT-LIB 2.6 from anthill knowledge bases (Z3 / CVC5 target). Today only rustland has this codegen: `rustland/anthill-smt-gen/src/{lib,outcome,policy,tactic_emit}.rs` (~2.1k LOC) plus integration tests. Reference spec: `docs/smtlib-forward-mapping.md`. v0 scope, mirroring rustland: discharge a single linear-arithmetic obligation by declaring user-asserted fact fields as Real constants, translating one named rule body to SMT-LIB, asserting the negation of an upper bound on the head, and proving unsat via Z3. Reference target: `examples/webots-modelling/lf1/safety_common.anthill` comm_delay_max (5 linear ops over 5 floats). Surface area: (a) tactic_emit — Z3 `(check-sat-using ...)` body emission with trivial-default elision parity; (b) policy — per-predicate TranslationPolicy fact lookup; (c) outcome — parse Z3 textual model + unsat-core into anthill facts (note: rustland already has S-expression in_string handling in outcome.rs:68-100 that scaland must mirror). Files: new sbt sub-project `scaland/anthill-smt-gen/{src/main/scala,src/test/scala}`, register in `scaland/build.sbt` aggregate. Acceptance: sbt test green; comm_delay_max round-trips through the scaland emitter and Z3 returns unsat byte-identically to rustland (or with a documented intentional divergence). Out of scope: proof cache (separate WI, depends on this one), quantifiers, induction, full reachability — those layer on top once v0 lands. Driver: parity with rustland realization story; needed before scaland can drive proof obligations end-to-end."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-143"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-09T21:39:49Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-213", author: "user", content: "v0 ports the comm_delay_max round-trip path: scaland/anthill-smt-gen/{Outcome,Policy,TacticEmit,SmtGen}.scala (~700 LOC) plus Common+Z3Runner test fixtures and CommDelayTest. 23/23 anthill-smt-gen tests green: 7 Outcome (S-expr in_string handling), 9 TacticEmit (runtime walker incl. trivial-default elision), 3 Policy (TranslationPolicy lookup), 4 CommDelay (well-formed doc, Z3 round-trip to unsat, config overrides, prefix-order arith). The Z3 round-trip on the 5-linear-op comm_delay_max obligation matches rustland: Z3 reports unsat byte-for-byte equivalent to the rustland emitter (modulo cosmetic whitespace). HeadShape classifier mirrors rustland post-WI-143 (Bottom / Predicate / FunctionLike / Unsupported); LabelFunctor arm dropped — scaland never produced the synthesized 0-arg label-functor shape (multi-head desugaring is a separate WI). One scaland-specific quirk surfaced: scaland Loader.scala only registers SymbolKind.Rule entries for labeled rules, so unlabeled function-like rules like `rule comm_delay_max(?tau) :- body` cant be looked up via `tryResolveSymbol` by their head functor name — adapted the test to use a labeled form `rule comm_delay_max: comm_delay_max(?tau) :- ...`. Out of scope for v0: lift_rule_to_implication_clause (proposal-031 cited-axiom emission), multi-pos-arg rule call inlining (try_inline_rule_call), fact-match fallback (try_match_fact_call), field-access resolution, proof cache (WI-214). simplify pass: dropped a `shortName(qualifiedNameOf)` helper in favor of `kb.resolveSym(sym)`, fixed 4 non-local-return compiler warnings, made SmtGenError a plain case class (no Exception inheritance), and an O(n²) regex-advance bug in extractDefineFuns. Acceptance: scaland sbt anthillSmtGen/test green; comm_delay_max round-trips to unsat. The 2 pre-existing scaland core test failures (anthill.codegen.scala.BootstrapTest::WI-170 and anthill.parse.ParserIntegrationTest::WI-153 stdlib float) are unchanged from origin/main baseline.", at: "2026-05-09T21:40:13Z")
